  "prefLabel": "En 1002.54 Utility",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "En 1002.54 “Utility” means the company that owns and operates the distribution facilities delivering electricity to the customer’s premises and subject to the jurisdiction of the department and the commission. For the purpose of this chapter, the term utility does not include a rural electric cooperative for which a certificate of deregulation is on file with the commission.\n\nSource. #14657, eff 9-1-26, EXPIRES: 9-1-36",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/en1000.html"
